close_reason: "Secret-guard findings have a stable category per rule and a default-plus-overrides policy helper, so a consumer that decides findings through the helper no longer breaks when a detector is added"
contract_change:
  api: "SecretGuardRule, SecretGuardRuleCategory, SecretGuardPolicy, SecretGuardPolicyDecision, SECRET_GUARD_RULE_CATEGORIES, secretGuardRuleCategory and decideSecretGuardFinding"
  before: "Typed consumers kept an exhaustive Record over the SecretGuardFinding rule union, so every new detector failed their compilation with TS2741"
  after: "Every detector has a stable credential, network or path category, and decideSecretGuardFinding decides a finding by precedence: a defined own rules entry, then the policy's defined entry for the rule's category, then the default (an undefined entry falls through), so a new detector without its own entry takes its category's decision or the default; an unchanged exhaustive Record over the rule union still breaks when a detector is added"
  migrate: "Replace an exhaustive Record over SecretGuardFinding['rule'] with a SecretGuardPolicy and decideSecretGuardFinding, or key an exhaustive map by SecretGuardRuleCategory"
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_strengthened
  owner: pm-gh1749
  gate_id: sdk-surface-snapshot
  negative_control: "Adding a category to the core SecretRuleCategory union without the SDK SecretGuardRuleCategory literal fails tsc (TS2322 on CATEGORY_SETS_MATCH in src/sdk/mutation-guard.ts), and the SDK surface snapshot now records the category literals, so a new category is classified as a breaking change; tests/unit/sdk/security/secret-guard-rule-categories.spec.ts pins every rule's category and proves a mocked future detector inherits its category decision"
  local_checks[3]: pnpm typecheck,node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/security/secret-guard-rule-categories.spec.ts,node scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs --check
  hosted_checks[2]: Gates (static),Gates (coverage)
body: ""
